  "full_text": "This is the tanks war game. We're going to use tournament settings and we're going to set animation delay to 50% and you can make artificial intelligent players to play against. I'll cover that after we look at the game. Anyway I'm going to do human against AI. So the first phase is a artillery plot. This is an artillery and the circle shows the range. So you try and anticipate your opponent's movements because the artillery lands after they move. Anyway you have two artillery pieces. This whole game is kind of not very good to be quite honest. Anyway I did it as kind of a demo. I get a demo of my operating system I guess. The red is roads, the blue is rivers. Anyway so you move around. Your tanks have stronger armor on the front and sides than they do on the rear. And now we're going to do shooting. So if you're curious you can get to know the way the battle is calculated. show odds. So you have to hit and then you have to roll. You have to it does a random number for damage. And this one didn't hit so it was a miss. Anyway I think this is a dumb game to be quite honest. But it shows the potential of the operating system. Anyway so I guess if you wanted you could make an AI player. So you put your AI I think you put it in your own directory. I forgot. Anyway so this fires at the nearest and moves toward the nearest. Technically you should obey the fog of war with your players. But I didn't even set up a API interface. So basically if you wanted to set up a artificial intelligence you go ahead and look at the original code to see how it works. Anyway well that's it. So sorry. you you you",
